<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Nahj al-Burda (Ahmad Shawqi)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">poem in a similar style</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Burdat Tamim (Tamim al-Barghouti)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2010</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new poem in the Burda line; published 2013, video series 2020</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Mantle Adorned (Timothy Winter)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tianfangshijing</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Chinese translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Commentaries by Ibn Hajar al-Haytami, Nazifi, Qastallani and others</span><span class="sg-chain-h">over 90 commentaries</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bānat Suʿād (Ka'b ibn Zuhayr)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">an earlier poem first called al-Burda (whether al-Busiri drew on it is not known)</span></li></ul></section>
